Hi [~accountid:6052891960d39e006f72f0f0] 

Please see below the answers to your questions:

*1.Is the market subject to laws where an employment relationship can be deemed or implied? yes/no*

{color:#bf2600}Yes.{color}

*2. Is there any evidence that platforms are under scrutiny under the legal system (litigation etc)*

{color:#bf2600}No.{color}

*3. Is the relevant test subject to express presumption criteria? yes/no*

{color:#bf2600}Yes.{color}

{color:#bf2600}Article 12 of the new employment law establishes that an employment contract shall be presumed to exist when, in the relationship between the activity provider and the digital platform some of the following characteristics are verified:{color}

{color:#bf2600}(a) the digital platform establishes the remuneration for the work carried out on the platform or establishes maximum and minimum limits for it;{color}

{color:#bf2600}(b) the digital platform exercises a power of direction and sets specific rules, in particular on how the provider of the activity behaves towards the user of the service or the provision of the activity;{color}

{color:#bf2600}(c) the digital platform controls and supervises the provision of the activity, including in real time, or checks the quality of the activity provided, in particular by electronic means or algorithmic management;{color}

{color:#bf2600}(d) the digital platform restricts the autonomy of the activity provider with regard to the organisation of work, in particular the choice of working time or of periods of absence, the possibility of accepting or refusing tasks, the use of subcontractors or substitutes, through the application of penalties, the choice of customers or to provide activity to third parties via a platform;{color}

{color:#bf2600}(e) the digital platform exercises labour powers over the activity provider,in particular disciplinary powers, including exclusion from further activity on the platform by deactivating the account;{color}

{color:#bf2600}(f) the work equipment and tools used belong to or are operated by the digital platform by means of a rental agreement.{color}

*4. Are reclassification sensitive activity expressly considered by a court or any law to imply an employment relationship?*

{color:#bf2600}The employment relationship between the driver/courier and the digital platform must be expressly declared by a Court as the presumption of employment established by the above mentioned law does not automatically apply.{color}

*5. Can claims be made in respect of past periods (i.e. for previously withheld earnings?)*

{color:#bf2600}Retroactive payments will be due as of commencement of employment, which is established by the Court, and usually refers to the commencement of the relationship between the courier and the digital platform. If the Court rules in favor of an employment contract on the 1st of August and the employment contract is confirmed to have commenced in January, retroactive payments will be due as of January, including, for example, potential wage differentials (if the worker received less than minimum wage), social security and tax charges, professional expenses, paid holidays, vacation and Christmas allowances, potential overtime, and potential night-time work compensation, if any.{color}

*6. Who is able to take action against Bolt? Couriers / group action / regulators*

{color:#bf2600}*Platform workers*{color}{color:#bf2600} may bring claims against a platform directly before court = {color}{color:#bf2600}+Employee’s lawsuit+{color}{color:#bf2600} → First instance judgment ETA is 8 months ; appeal phase ETA is 8-10 months.{color}

{color:#bf2600}*ACT*{color}{color:#bf2600} (Labour inspector) may notify the platform to recognize the worker as a subordinate employee and regularize the situation. Then either:{color}

# {color:#bf2600}The platform regularizes the employee's situation by presenting an employment contract: the procedure is then closed immediately - however administrative offenses under Art.12 and 12-A of the Labour Code are possible (fines up to € 61K); or{color}
# {color:#bf2600}If the platform doesn’ regularize the worker’s situation within 10 days, ACT has 5 days to send a report to the Public Prosecutor's Office requesting to institute proceedings and then the Public Prosecutor's Office has 20 days to file the {color}{color:#bf2600}+proceedings for recognition of the existence of an employment contract+{color}{color:#bf2600}.{color}

{color:#bf2600}*Social Security* {color}{color:#bf2600}may also promote the administrative offense procedure within the scope of the social security system (pursuant to Law no. 107/2009).{color}

*7. Is there any evidence the authorities have considered couriers eligible for employment benefits in the past (e.g. tax authorities, pension authorities etc)?*

{color:#bf2600}No.{color}

*8. What is the level of access to justice in a market (e.g. high state duties, requirement to have a representative etc)?*

{color:#bf2600}Labour jurisdiction is easily accessible for workers in Portugal, as legal representation is not compulsory and no court fees apply. In addition, many workers are entitled to social security legal aid (very common for employees with union membership and/or low wages).{color}

*9. Can claims be made to reclassify all couriers of the platform in a market at once?*

{color:#bf2600}No, the above described proceeding must be followed for each specific worker of each specific platform. {color}{color:#bf2600}*No mass reclassifications are foreseen*{color}{color:#bf2600}. Each situation will be assessed on a case-by-case basis.{color}

----

Should you have any further questions, please do let me know.

Thank you.

