the cache is updated in *order/driver/service/OrderService* in 3 different ways:


1. *manually*, with commands such as:

{noformat}await this.orderCacheUpdater.update(ctx, orderId).catch(() => {});
await this.orderTryCacheUpdater.updateOrderTry(ctx, [orderTry.order_try_id]).catch(() => {});{noformat}

This happens in {{setDestinations}} and {{selectNextStop}} method



2. via *EvolveOrderService:*

{{evolveOrderService.syncCache()}}
which in turn does the following:

{noformat}await this.orderTryCacheUpdater.updateOrderTry(ctx, orderTryIds).catch(() => {});
for (const driverId of driverIds) {
    await this.driverStateCacheUpdater.update(ctx, driverId).catch(() => {}); // never fail
}
for (const req of syncCacheRequest.data) {
    await this.orderCacheUpdater.update(ctx, req.order_id).catch(() => {});
}{noformat}



3. via *orderCore* methods (eg: orderDepartFromStop) that call *OrderStopService* that calls *OrderStopCacheUpdater*, with commands such as:

{{OrderStopCacheUpdater.updateOrderOrderTryAndDriverStateCache}}

which in turn does the following:


{noformat}(onEachCtx) => this.orderCacheUpdater.update(onEachCtx, orderId).catch(() => {}),
(onEachCtx) => this.orderTryCacheUpdater.updateOrderTry(onEachCtx, [orderTryId]).catch(() => {}),
(onEachCtx) => this.driverStateCacheUpdater.update(onEachCtx, driverId).catch(() => {}){noformat}



----

* *group 1* makes cache updates through {{orderCacheUpdater}} and {{orderTryCacheUpdater}}
* *group 2 + 3* make cache updates through {{orderCacheUpdater}}, {{orderTryCacheUpdater}} and {{driverStateCacheUpdater}}

-SOLUTION? → add driverStateCacheUpdater updates to group 1 calls- → no as DriverCache has no order

*order/driver/service/OrderService* has {{setPriceInternal}} method.
At the end tries to update the cache calling {{this.evolveOrderService.driverSetRidePrice}}

Inside the method there is [this part|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/develop/src/rides/marketplace/order/main/commonV2/order/OrderPriceService.ts#L177-L185]:

{noformat}await this.driverStateService.bumpNextB2BOrderVersion(ctx, params.driver_id, params.order_id);

if (stateUpdateResult) {
