Hi [~accountid:5c6bbd9d00a665752ca2c9e8] 

Thanks for your patience whilst we looked into your questions above, this [RFC|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nxpraqtyZcxPZXFVuioDLAxqhmqCdYMeTjdKSxE6i7Q/edit#heading=h.2pscjlpmwit9] and the [Badger Bot Confluence Page|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DATA/pages/4374921404/Badger+Bot].

As the business has been using both versions of the tool (API and ChatGPT), we have reviewed both sets of privacy terms that apply to each product and summarised our advice in the attached [document|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tdvvidXTBooMwa1Tzmv-Q1CoErwjEdQ2G22BDVBBDMA/edit]. 

To summarise, my recommendation after having consulted with Matheus is: 

* *ChatGPT* - should not be used by Bolt for processing rider/eater/courier/driver/employee personal data, internal use data, restricted data and confidential data (as described in the [+Data Classification Policy+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ISO/pages/1969619299/Data+Classification+Policy]). This includes using the tool for the activities you outlined in the RFC and above i.e. content creation, moderation, summarisation, analysing feedback, writing/correcting source code, summarise text. Recommend we issue a company-wide statement/guidance advising against the use of ChatGPT and reiterating that if there are specific projects requiring the use of OpenAi’s ChatGPT tool then these need to be approved first before being used. Provided you / management are aligned with this approach, Matheus/I will work with Comms to prepare this communication. 
* *API* - can be used provided you/management are comfortable with risks outlined in the attached and we take the following steps:  
** we virtually sign the Data Processing Addendum with OpenAI - need to confirm if this can be signed by me or has to be signed by Ahto on behalf of Bolt;
** we opt out of OpenAI using our data for their own purposes - to be completed by you;
** we sign up for notifications of new sub-processors being used by OpenAI - to be completed by my team;
** we prepare guidance for safe use of the tool (i.e. do’s and don’ts) which your team and others using the API must follow. This would also apply to Badger Bot and all the project ideas you’ve outlined in the RFC. I’ve started a draft but this will require input from you, Comms, People and Info Sec teams - will share asap; 
** we complete a transfer impact assessment to cover the transfer of data from the EEA/UK to the US - this will be done by my team;
** we identify if any changes are needed to our Employee Privacy Notice - this will depend on what employee personal data you intend to input into the tool; 
** we identify if any changes are needed to our externally-facing Rider/Driver/Passenger Privacy Notices - this will depend on what personal data relating to these groups of individuals you intend to input into the tool; and
** we review their security terms - I believe Tarmo’s team will review these and flag any additional steps we need to take from a security perspective. This is particularly important given OpenAI has already suffered a data breach of it’s ChatGPT tool. 

The use of both of these tools is not risk-free given the regulatory focus on OpenAI at the moment and the rapidly changing regulatory landscape. However, if we take the steps above associated with our use of the API tools this will help to mitigate (not eliminate) all of the risks and in the meantime, my team and the DPO team will continue to monitor the regulatory situation and let you know if there are any developments which mean we’ll need to take a different approach. 

Hope this is all clear, if you have any questions let me know.

Thanks

Sam

